WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Follow Jordan, an example executive, through the complete content

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:09.440
journey. The workspace has four stages: Describe, Personalize, Create

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.400
and review, and Publish. Each stage has one main

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.820
action, and you can go back at any time.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.480
Developers keep the detailed controls under Advanced settings, where

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.600
connected agents such as Codex and Claude Code work

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.280
in the same workspace. Nothing is published without your

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:27.660
own click.

00:00:29.145 --> 00:00:32.885
Jordan advises healthcare leaders and wants a weekly evidence

00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:35.665
briefing, with a short video in their own voice.

00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:39.285
Describe your audience and topic in a few sentences.

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:42.925
Choose the writer that will draft the words, using

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:46.665
an account already connected on this computer, and choose

00:00:46.665 --> 00:00:49.745
the narration: your own local voice, or a built-in

00:00:49.745 --> 00:00:52.545
narrator. Then continue to personalize.

00:00:54.068 --> 00:00:57.528
Personalize asks only the choices that change the result:

00:00:57.528 --> 00:01:00.948
your logo, a style direction, how long the newsletter

00:01:00.948 --> 00:01:04.128
and the video should be, the video format, and

00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:08.268
how often you publish. Every unfamiliar choice shows a

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:12.428
recommendation with its reason. Use recommendations fills what you

00:01:12.428 --> 00:01:15.628
have not decided, and never replaces a choice you

00:01:15.628 --> 00:01:19.468
already made. Your logo appears in the newsletter and

00:01:19.468 --> 00:01:20.688
at the end of every video.

00:01:22.158 --> 00:01:25.358
For a conversation, a panel, or a product pitch,

00:01:25.878 --> 00:01:28.858
name the people who will present. Each presenter has

00:01:28.858 --> 00:01:32.078
a role, an approved voice, and a recorded consent.

00:01:32.838 --> 00:01:36.658
Two presenters make a host and expert conversation; three

00:01:36.658 --> 00:01:39.458
make a panel or a pitch. The video shows

00:01:39.458 --> 00:01:42.418
who is speaking, and if any presenter’s voice fails

00:01:42.418 --> 00:01:45.718
to render, the draft holds rather than switching identity.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.370
Create and review makes one private package: a sourced

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:54.950
newsletter and a narrated video about the same stories.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.670
Your progress stays visible, and if you reload the

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:02.270
page the work resumes instead of starting over. For

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:05.230
this walkthrough we use a labelled teaching package with

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:08.710
the finished sample video, rather than generating a factual

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:12.870
healthcare story. In your workspace, inspect the actual sources,

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:14.350
words and narration.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:20.315
Before any narration is recorded, the workspace pauses and

00:02:20.315 --> 00:02:22.935
offers each story only what its own source supports:

00:02:22.935 --> 00:02:27.175
the actual news image, an attributed headline card, or

00:02:27.175 --> 00:02:31.695
an explanation diagram that passed a phone-size check. News

00:02:31.695 --> 00:02:36.695
about people and institutions recommends the reporting image. Rights

00:02:36.695 --> 00:02:39.635
are stated plainly, and you can upload an image

00:02:39.635 --> 00:02:43.195
you own. Accept the recommendations, or choose for each

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:45.035
story, and production continues.

00:02:46.728 --> 00:02:49.328
When the package is ready, the video and the

00:02:49.328 --> 00:02:53.048
newsletter open on this same page. Watch the video,

00:02:53.388 --> 00:02:56.088
read the newsletter, and check that every visual looks

00:02:56.088 --> 00:03:00.428
publishable. Story visuals carry their evidence and are shared

00:03:00.428 --> 00:03:03.968
by the newsletter and the video. Failed checks never

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:07.748
appear inside your newsletter; a rejected visual cannot reach

00:03:07.748 --> 00:03:09.568
review or approval at all.

00:03:11.032 --> 00:03:14.252
Now see the finished product. These are three real

00:03:14.252 --> 00:03:18.212
renders of the same short briefing: narrated slides, presenter

00:03:18.212 --> 00:03:22.892
only, and presenter alongside slides. The presenter is fictional

00:03:22.892 --> 00:03:26.592
and AI generated. Narrated slides are available in Free.

00:03:27.652 --> 00:03:30.552
Presenter production is a Pro option, with setup handled

00:03:30.552 --> 00:03:34.492
behind the scenes by MyOwnAI Labs. You choose the

00:03:34.492 --> 00:03:39.012
result, without navigating animation vendors. Watch the same content

00:03:39.012 --> 00:03:39.812
in each layout.

00:03:41.525 --> 00:03:45.105
start with reliable sources. Check each claim,

00:03:45.665 --> 00:03:48.165
review the finished video, and publish only

00:03:48.165 --> 00:03:51.085
when you are ready. Then use audience

00:03:51.085 --> 00:03:53.225
feedback to improve your next briefing.

00:03:55.387 --> 00:04:00.267
Publish begins with your destinations. Jordan selects LinkedIn and

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:04.107
YouTube together. Each channel shows plainly whether it is

00:04:04.107 --> 00:04:08.187
connected, ready to connect, or still needs setup in

00:04:08.187 --> 00:04:12.087
Developer tools. Save the destinations you will actually use.

00:04:12.687 --> 00:04:15.347
You can make and review a private preview before

00:04:15.347 --> 00:04:18.587
connecting any publishing account, and nothing is sent to

00:04:18.587 --> 00:04:19.947
a channel by saving this list.

00:04:21.484 --> 00:04:24.624
Preview is the beginning of review, not the end

00:04:24.624 --> 00:04:27.944
of the engine. Open the exact package, watch the

00:04:27.944 --> 00:04:31.524
video and read the companion newsletter. Approve only that

00:04:31.524 --> 00:04:35.864
exact version. A changed package needs fresh approval; team

00:04:35.864 --> 00:04:39.924
workspaces can require another reviewer. The next controls publish

00:04:39.924 --> 00:04:43.164
the newsletter, post the approved video to a selected

00:04:43.164 --> 00:04:46.124
channel, and add its link back to the newsletter.

00:04:47.044 --> 00:04:50.324
Each external action needs its own explicit browser click.

00:04:50.324 --> 00:04:52.964
We do not publish this demonstration.

00:04:54.538 --> 00:04:58.178
After publishing, open Results. Delivery tells you whether a

00:04:58.178 --> 00:05:01.918
channel accepted the post. Independent checks confirm the published

00:05:01.918 --> 00:05:06.718
post. An uncertain attempt needs inspection, not an automatic

00:05:06.718 --> 00:05:11.778
retry. Audience analytics show what happened next: views, engagement

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:15.338
and the channels that responded. The numbers shown here

00:05:15.338 --> 00:05:19.398
are clearly labelled training data. Missing measurements remain unknown.

00:05:20.158 --> 00:05:23.178
Growing the publication with these results is an optional

00:05:23.178 --> 00:05:23.738
Pro service.

00:05:25.359 --> 00:05:29.499
The engine continues into audience follow-up. Questions and corrections

00:05:29.499 --> 00:05:32.699
rise to the top of the inbox. Review a

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:36.519
viewer’s response, prepare a helpful reply, and approve its

00:05:36.519 --> 00:05:40.279
exact wording before sending. Your agent can suggest a

00:05:40.279 --> 00:05:44.019
draft; it cannot grant approval. X and YouTube support

00:05:44.019 --> 00:05:49.279
account-authorized collection and replies. Other channels use manual capture

00:05:49.279 --> 00:05:53.979
and posting handoff. Reactions help identify interest, but do

00:05:53.979 --> 00:05:55.099
not create reply threads.

00:05:56.673 --> 00:06:00.953
The cost dashboard shows recorded writing-model calls, reported dollar

00:06:00.953 --> 00:06:05.453
amounts, and calls whose prices were not returned. These

00:06:05.453 --> 00:06:08.733
example entries are training data, not your bill. Unknown

00:06:08.733 --> 00:06:12.433
is not zero. This dashboard does not yet meter

00:06:12.433 --> 00:06:18.113
agent subscriptions, conversation, voice, avatar, rendering or tunnel charges.

00:06:18.773 --> 00:06:21.893
Check those account statements for the full cost. Use

00:06:21.893 --> 00:06:25.353
this view to understand recorded usage while keeping those

00:06:25.353 --> 00:06:26.073
limits visible.

00:06:27.618 --> 00:06:30.778
Developers can offer writers that run on this computer.

00:06:31.298 --> 00:06:34.258
Every model Ollama has downloaded appears in the writer

00:06:34.258 --> 00:06:38.258
list, with its status beside it. The editorial qualification

00:06:38.258 --> 00:06:41.878
classifies a fixed slate of stories, writes a script

00:06:41.878 --> 00:06:45.038
inside the word budget, and plans a visual, twice,

00:06:45.038 --> 00:06:48.738
inside a time ceiling, and records a durable pass

00:06:48.738 --> 00:06:52.358
or fail for that exact model and machine. A

00:06:52.358 --> 00:06:55.818
model that has not passed can still create previews,

00:06:55.818 --> 00:06:59.698
and the connected-account fallback finishes any draft it cannot.

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:04.527
Use the results and audience questions to refine your

00:07:04.527 --> 00:07:09.067
next edition. Update your choices in Personalize, ask your

00:07:09.067 --> 00:07:12.707
agents to investigate the strongest questions, and prepare a

00:07:12.707 --> 00:07:16.047
new private draft. Talk to your harness is an

00:07:16.047 --> 00:07:19.907
optional conversation space with microphone controls and a transcript.

00:07:20.547 --> 00:07:23.627
You can interrupt or type during a connected session.

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:28.887
Its voice connection is separate from publication narration. Final

00:07:28.887 --> 00:07:31.567
approvals and external actions stay in the browser.

00:07:33.101 --> 00:07:35.351
Book a demo at My Own AI Labs dot

00:07:35.201 --> 00:07:39.061
com. Bring your use case, and we’ll estimate the

00:07:39.061 --> 00:07:42.141
hours you could save each week. The open-source engine

00:07:42.141 --> 00:07:45.841
is free. Pro is planned at ninety-nine dollars a

00:07:45.841 --> 00:07:50.301
month for premium workflows and guided support. Agent subscriptions

00:07:50.301 --> 00:07:51.861
and usage are separate.
